    <fr:title text="The Fredholm ledger">The Fredholm ledger</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
    <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="thread">ns</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>For a tall split with flanks <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\widetilde {L}]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\widetilde {R}]]></fr:tex>, the ledger is
exact: <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link> holds if and only if <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  N_{\mathrm {weak}} \le  N_z + \binom {v+1}{2},
]]></fr:tex>
while <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[N_{\mathrm {weak}} \le  N_{\mathrm {strict}} + \binom {v+1}{2}]]></fr:tex> is automatic. Hence
multi-block <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link> follows from <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0045/" title="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/" display-uri="ffi-0045" type="local">(NS)</fr:link>.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> The extension-module theorem: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\ker  \Phi _c^*]]></fr:tex> is the space
of strict <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {Hom}_\Lambda (\widetilde {L}, \widetilde {R})]]></fr:tex>-triples with a <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\binom {v+1}{2}]]></fr:tex>
belowdiagonal relaxation, of dimension
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\hom (\tilde \lambda , \tilde \mu ) - v^2 + \binom {v+1}{2}]]></fr:tex>. The
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[G]]></fr:tex>-identity gives
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\dim  G = \hom (\tilde \lambda , \tilde \mu ) - \hom (\lambda , \mu )]]></fr:tex>, and
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {codim} R I_c = \operatorname {rank} P]]></fr:tex> by trace duality. The five-equation centralizer
system then computes <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\dim  z_q(y)]]></fr:tex> bit-exactly
(ns_lift.sage), reducing everything to one rank identity <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \operatorname {rank}(B, C, D) = \operatorname {rank}(D') + n_L v + v n_R.
]]></fr:tex></html:p>
    <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0042/" title="Splits, flanks, tallness" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0042/" display-uri="ffi-0042" type="local">Splits, flanks, tallness</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0044/" title="Tall-Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0044/" display-uri="ffi-0044" type="local">Tall-Lemma V</fr:link>.</html:p>
    <html:p>
      <html:em>Provenance: result13_addendum.md; mb_dual.sage and .log 13/13 equality;
ns_lift.sage.</html:em>
    </html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
