            <fr:title text="Splits, flanks, tallness">Splits, flanks, tallness</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>definition</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="thread">ns</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>A <html:em>split</html:em> of a composition <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c = (c_L, v, c_R)]]></fr:tex>
isolates a middle block of size <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[v]]></fr:tex> — the longest part, +1 convention —
with flanks <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c_L]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c_R]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p>The split is <html:em>tall</html:em> if <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \max (c_L) \ge  v \quad  \text {and} \quad  \max (c_R) \ge  v,
]]></fr:tex>
and <html:em>dominated</html:em> if moreover <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c_L[-1] > v]]></fr:tex> and
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c_R[0] > v]]></fr:tex>. The three classes nest: dominated <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\subset ]]></fr:tex> dip
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\subset ]]></fr:tex> tall.</html:p>
            <html:p>Write <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c']]></fr:tex> for the reductive quotient datum of a split, and
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\widetilde {L}]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\widetilde {R}]]></fr:tex> for the flanks with the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[v]]></fr:tex> longest parts
incremented — the modules <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0046/" title="The Fredholm ledger" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0046/" display-uri="ffi-0046" type="local">the Fredholm ledger</fr:link> is computed
in.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0028/" title="U-modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0028/" display-uri="ffi-0028" type="local">U-modality</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: result13_addendum.md 13(f)--(l).</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
