        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0042/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0042</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0042/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Splits, flanks, tallness">Splits, flanks, tallness</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>definition</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="thread">ns</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>A <html:em>split</html:em> of a composition <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c = (c_L, v, c_R)]]></fr:tex>
isolates a middle block of size <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[v]]></fr:tex> — the longest part, +1 convention —
with flanks <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c_L]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c_R]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p>The split is <html:em>tall</html:em> if <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \max (c_L) \ge  v \quad  \text {and} \quad  \max (c_R) \ge  v,
]]></fr:tex>
and <html:em>dominated</html:em> if moreover <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c_L[-1] > v]]></fr:tex> and
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c_R[0] > v]]></fr:tex>. The three classes nest: dominated <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\subset ]]></fr:tex> dip
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\subset ]]></fr:tex> tall.</html:p>
            <html:p>Write <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c']]></fr:tex> for the reductive quotient datum of a split, and
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\widetilde {L}]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\widetilde {R}]]></fr:tex> for the flanks with the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[v]]></fr:tex> longest parts
incremented — the modules <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0046/" title="The Fredholm ledger" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0046/" display-uri="ffi-0046" type="local">the Fredholm ledger</fr:link> is computed
in.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0028/" title="U-modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0028/" display-uri="ffi-0028" type="local">U-modality</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: result13_addendum.md 13(f)--(l).</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0044/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0044</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0044/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Tall-Lemma V">Tall-Lemma V</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="thread">ns</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>For every <html:em>tall</html:em> split, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link> holds with equality.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Zero violations in 11,452 tall splits, against 958 failures all
of which are off-tall (tall_exact2.log).</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> Tallness is exactly the scope, and the three cases say why.
Dominated splits carry the gain in the kernel of the fibration map
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Theta ]]></fr:tex>, where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\dim  \ker  \Theta  = v^2]]></fr:tex>; tall-not-dominated carry it
in the image; off-tall breaks the balance by exactly <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[+1]]></fr:tex>, an S-mode
through <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\ker  \alpha ]]></fr:tex>. The <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Q]]></fr:tex>-fibration machinery of
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0047/" title="(Q-MOD): the reductive repair" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0047/" display-uri="ffi-0047" type="local">(Q-MOD)</fr:link> consumes precisely tallness and nothing more.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0042/" title="Splits, flanks, tallness" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0042/" display-uri="ffi-0042" type="local">Splits, flanks, tallness</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: result13_addendum.md 13(f)--(l); ns_theta.log,
tall_exact2.py and .log, dip_exact.py and .log. Note tall_exact2,
dip_exact and ns_session_state were lost pre-commit and regenerated from
umod_tables.tsv, reproducing the cited numbers exactly.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
